review:
​[h1]Star Wars - Knights of the Old Republic[/h1]

[u]Verdict[/u]: set thousands of years before Episode I, KotOR is a timeless RPG and shouldn't be missed for any reason, even 15 years after its release. The main aspects that drew me in were the story and its setting, interacting with other characters and seeing them develop while being affected by my own choices. Other than that, the game offers up its share of fun puzzles and combat (which, despite appearances, is actually a turn-based system) framed in a fairly familiar classes/skill points system.

[b]Pros:[/b]
[list]
[*]Involving, open-ended story (with some good use of choices);
[*]Great use of classic Star Wars setting through various locations;
[*]Interesting side quests and fun(-ish) mini-games;
[*]Graphics hold up well (for a game first released in 2003!);
[*]Well-voiced set of party characters, some of which offer interesting duality;
[*]Original (for the most part) soundtrack suits the atmosphere well.
[/list]
[b]Cons:[/b]
[list]
[*]Ally AI is pretty clueless at times and movement can be a bit clumsy;
[*]Pazaak "randomness" is wildly uneven in favour of NPCs;
[*]Tedious envirosuit sequences;
[*]Travel between worlds being interupted by the shooting mini-game quickly becomes annoying;
[*]Some bugs, glitches and crashes.
[/list]
